{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-behavioral_generation-01", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:behavioral_generation-1"], "facet": "behavioral_generation", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "Each completion record retains the original prompt, generated string, stop reason, and decoding seed so exact output behavior can be examined again.", "text_sha256": "e312975bde8277dff7872bbf1d0c26de45e9850c132ded77951dd60b3217f830"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-behavioral_generation-02", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:behavioral_generation-2"], "facet": "behavioral_generation", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A model may emit tokens reliably yet fail the requested task, so completion length and instruction fit are evaluated separately.", "text_sha256": "d468f4b24a9f365d3f70695969e21e0b9f21a31958b91a76ad8be242630d25dd"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-behavioral_generation-03", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:behavioral_generation-3"], "facet": "behavioral_generation", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "The final response audit stores raw model output before any human formatting or correction is applied.", "text_sha256": "076b350184e56118a17d90c66d7d6c36fa888f7b5b2c563d68f3dd2360a22c5b"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-behavioral_generation-04", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:behavioral_generation-4"], "facet": "behavioral_generation", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A refusal, an empty answer, and a truncated completion are distinct generation outcomes and should not share one label.", "text_sha256": "d4dc3fb55c79180cc6f9675c9e291a9586fe11ac099012b87bbe42208577f694"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-next_token_statistics-01", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:next_token_statistics-1"], "facet": "next_token_statistics", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "Likelihood is calculated over observed target units and reported with the number of UTF-8 bytes actually scored.", "text_sha256": "1977c2675115cc8ad769069357266dd174ef6cf7f99942aeffd3a7bf02362d28"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-next_token_statistics-02", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:next_token_statistics-2"], "facet": "next_token_statistics", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "Cross-tokenizer comparisons normalize the same string because a single word may split into multiple native tokens.", "text_sha256": "3e0644ce0fcae32660ece872aa9ad3cae35d65e8f9e20df50c542185f77679da"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-next_token_statistics-03", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:next_token_statistics-3"], "facet": "next_token_statistics", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "The score file stores the target prefix and model hash so another run can recreate the loss denominator.", "text_sha256": "a2c951ec7e4dae8421432978ac997ec028fd162b8283aa0b1f5a861d0dbcfa05"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-next_token_statistics-04", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:next_token_statistics-4"], "facet": "next_token_statistics", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A top-token match is a local prediction result and does not by itself establish that a full answer is correct.", "text_sha256": "3e54ff144bcb4e466cad3ff04ca999e7392499b1d890f168d87fa45561675703"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-hidden_representations-01", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:hidden_representations-1"], "facet": "hidden_representations", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "The probe stores layerwise vectors for a fixed token position and model revision so representation differences can be replayed.", "text_sha256": "fcef5ec7f2f4dc321cccc167fbb9adea0f2071def1e24ad11c04482abfe909ee"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-hidden_representations-02", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:hidden_representations-2"], "facet": "hidden_representations", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A hidden coordinate receives a feature label only after a contrastive prediction and intervention are tested independently.", "text_sha256": "6cc2cee1c4f984633af1867d137a6618a401de6b95966110a062ff3b48c93e4a"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-hidden_representations-03", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:hidden_representations-3"], "facet": "hidden_representations", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "The activation tensor shape and numeric range are recorded before a semantic interpretation is proposed.", "text_sha256": "789f164507687544e67a812a1dccbebf85b96194c025f0c91131d0214fb0ec61"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-hidden_representations-04", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:hidden_representations-4"], "facet": "hidden_representations", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "An observed vector may support multiple downstream operations, so one dimension is not automatically a named concept.", "text_sha256": "85a13d12763b06782ddda5dce2f3425a6c5f19ec53bf5f26589847ecff4c26a5"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-attention_patterns-01", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:attention_patterns-1"], "facet": "attention_patterns", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "The observed attention matrix is indexed by query and key positions after application of the causal mask.", "text_sha256": "08d47357b7218c2a0a81a565db825e7703a210ad92394bf015035bdcdc4ea491"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-attention_patterns-02", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:attention_patterns-2"], "facet": "attention_patterns", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "Head entropy describes one activation trace and does not certify the purpose of that attention head.", "text_sha256": "400994e8faceb82dff9453abf1446c23a93957f87a951cd00d3ca9c3ea8d11e2"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-attention_patterns-03", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:attention_patterns-3"], "facet": "attention_patterns", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A model without an attention operator is recorded as unavailable for head analysis rather than assigned an empty measured map.", "text_sha256": "9ec765cb474b34acbb4fa010c9b8464d7d73a9fa163523c2e61b29c8a0c9e426"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-attention_patterns-04", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:attention_patterns-4"], "facet": "attention_patterns", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "Layerwise attention comparisons require aligned input tokens and should retain the exact sequence used for capture.", "text_sha256": "b40c8e2ca29d486ad5770740e7a6c8f827c5ddaba85c6c6baa3ce283d6472ec6"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-ablation_response-01", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:ablation_response-1"], "facet": "ablation_response", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "Removing a block residual update preserves the incoming stream while testing dependence on the block learned transformation.", "text_sha256": "0179c1af2d3260da7c9f55c1ba38b40069923eed6922310e93d400f857e30bb1"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-ablation_response-02", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:ablation_response-2"], "facet": "ablation_response", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A prediction change after ablation is stored alongside the continuous logit difference from the baseline run.", "text_sha256": "61c1cb94061cf67fec0b4b042e551cb302414677415f3b74e881c5a5d8dcad07"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-ablation_response-03", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:ablation_response-3"], "facet": "ablation_response", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A control intervention targets a neighboring block to test whether the observed effect is location-specific.", "text_sha256": "2464e599cd82337679415a7b613eb2bf6cb3da694bebfd87cfb8bb2c759c968a"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-ablation_response-04", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:ablation_response-4"], "facet": "ablation_response", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "The intervention record includes the target operation and model hash so the internal perturbation can be reproduced.", "text_sha256": "61b635ac2a1daac7f4769d8ec1cfb0692d936f4c9ca45bc59863415191f3d9a9"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-scaling_response-01", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:scaling_response-1"], "facet": "scaling_response", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "The intervention sweep compares fixed coefficients while prompt, model weights, and decoding settings remain unchanged.", "text_sha256": "6e809fd9a3b3cb3d6619fa03847acac8d9a2fa4e0699deff98a3e2c3ef13e083"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-scaling_response-02", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:scaling_response-2"], "facet": "scaling_response", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A no-op coefficient provides a control for unexpected numerical changes during the scaling procedure.", "text_sha256": "deb27c167c9a015c42a8fc682a50067a89800e47aecd2e93109c063af543f442"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-scaling_response-03", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:scaling_response-3"], "facet": "scaling_response", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "Continuous logit movement can be measurable even when the identity of the highest-scoring token does not change.", "text_sha256": "7ce40dff4336b3cc79c9c95a0d8ecb6ed5d9a55f7cbafec6c1e16caaba59a092"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-scaling_response-04", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:scaling_response-4"], "facet": "scaling_response", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "The scale coefficient is recorded with the target path and baseline output to distinguish it from a constant replacement.", "text_sha256": "03524fdf43d3ad7460298dd897710186087425e762beaf6ee08d9bebbc2b6c7b"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-cross_language_behavior-01", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:cross_language_behavior-1"], "facet": "cross_language_behavior", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "The evaluation report preserves a separate score for each language instead of merging script-specific behavior into one aggregate.", "text_sha256": "93a81bf12222e7a59936ce8ec39dcf3385926c0cdc81a4d5e27dbd4694e0c047"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-cross_language_behavior-02", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:cross_language_behavior-2"], "facet": "cross_language_behavior", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A tokenizer may accept an unfamiliar script even when generated sequences in that language remain poor.", "text_sha256": "32fb940c90fe9ef973ab7c36dc71f766bb37474688f9c4372247a2e4378c91ec"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-cross_language_behavior-03", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:cross_language_behavior-3"], "facet": "cross_language_behavior", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "Language coverage and task correctness are measured separately because successful tokenization is not evidence of fluency.", "text_sha256": "9272525e8cc944f8f4990bcf3deb12cfd2fea2db4b411a662f6d467e6df7af17"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-cross_language_behavior-04", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:cross_language_behavior-4"], "facet": "cross_language_behavior", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A cross-language result includes the exact prompt, raw continuation, tokenizer identity, and evaluated byte count.", "text_sha256": "b62474d3ac8971c2d61403621414eb486a9c345daf48ddc75e83407da5356111"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-limitations_hypotheses-01", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:limitations_hypotheses-1"], "facet": "limitations_hypotheses", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "An effect observed on one prompt supports a narrow conclusion until it repeats across independent prompts and tasks.", "text_sha256": "6664e377c067b4c97dab630f27400bd0629493f0a0484a8cabfeffd40272fece"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-limitations_hypotheses-02", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:limitations_hypotheses-2"], "facet": "limitations_hypotheses", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "An interpretation remains provisional when several different causal paths could explain the same visible output.", "text_sha256": "1adfbe03f8cdb8f98ca5267b55e5101f6faf1fc1ebc6e90ec85ac76c34e942fc"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-limitations_hypotheses-03", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:limitations_hypotheses-3"], "facet": "limitations_hypotheses", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "The scope of a claim must not exceed the architectures, prompts, interventions, and language domains actually tested.", "text_sha256": "dd9839210fe7840d630162383dc1cb063b694a6ec72bab2ec8a36da036ac85b9"}
{"document_id": "MV31-FINAL-limitations_hypotheses-04", "evidence_ids": ["authored:fresh-final-test:limitations_hypotheses-4"], "facet": "limitations_hypotheses", "language": "en", "split": "test", "text": "A lower loss on a constructed corpus does not establish general reasoning or equivalent internal mechanisms.", "text_sha256": "432d7893b877ad8410ebe5e9d904bac134e24af237dada6d98de3e1c39c03fd3"}
